//Additions:
//-New Functions!
//  +mktypeText() <aniframe.h>
//  +strnull() <string++>
//  +scmath_pow10() <scmath.h>
//
//  +aprintf() was re-implemented and re-modeled.
//  +officially added new packages: 'misc.h',
//   'version.h', 'langpak.h'.
//  +implemented 2 more operators to 'oprpack.h'.
//  +now it's possible to verify the current version
//   & language thanks to 'version.h' & 'langpak.h'.
//  +implemented new cross-compatible compiler attributes
//   in 'attribs.h': 'aligned', 'format' and 'auto'. along
//   with a new special extension, "xsc_crossformat" that
//   automatically adapts the printing format for the user,
//   and many extra extensions & tokens for specific
//   pre-defined sections & custom sections.
//   +"finished" the aprintf and scmath_pow10 functions.
//   +re-implemented many functions back to scmath.h,
//    together with new ones.
//   +added back some functions into misc.h. among them,
      brought back the now slightly optimized concatf().
//Changes:
//  -2 syntax errors related to compiler.h fixed. (F-C0)
//  -changed preprocessor tag name back from 'CONFIG' to 'XSCCONF'.
//  -fixed a definition name flaw in 'compiler.h' in MSVC section. (F-A0)
//  -all the simplified types from keyword pack were
//   separated into a new package called simplified-t.h
//  -officially adopted the multi-line comment standard for C-89
//   soon, all the comments will be replaced with the multi-line model.
//   (even some comments are already starting to be replaced by multi-line comments
//   or adapted for C-89 standards.)
//   NOTE: some still need to be updated.
//  -finished the var keyword.
//  -replaced the string system in kwpack.h, now 'string' was renamed to 'mstring'
//   while 'ustring' became 'string', but 'ustring' it kinda makes more sense for
//   ustring to take it's place.
//  -huge code polishment.
//  -fixed another syntax flaw, this time floating related and on "getos". <stdbasic-getos.h> (F-C0)
//  -the name 'stdcleanup.h' was changed to 'libcrt.h' due to name convenience reasons.